│ patch_name               │ enhanced_margin_ansatz                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ The current program has excellent parameter efficiency (3 distinct params) and low depth  │
│                          │ (12), but critically fails on the worst_group_margin_mean (0.00), which directly limits   │
│                          │ the combined score despite good generalization gap (0.07). The goal is to improve robust  │
│                          │ separation on hard samples without sacrificing parameter efficiency.                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Analysis of prior programs:                                                               │
│                          │ 1. First program (score 0.29): 24 distinct params, high overfitting (gap 0.31), but       │
│                          │ worst_group_margin 0.03                                                                   │
│                          │ 2. Second program (score 0.40): 3 distinct params, lower gap (0.16), worst_group_margin   │
│                          │ 0.02                                                                                      │
│                          │ 3. Current (score 0.42): 3 distinct params, minimal gap (0.07), but worst_group_margin    │
│                          │ dropped to 0.00                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The worst_group_margin collapse suggests the current architecture cannot separate the     │
│                          │ hardest samples at all. The solution is to add structured non-uniformity while preserving │
│                          │ parameter sharing:                                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Strategy:                                                                                 │
│                          │ - Keep the aggressive parameter sharing (3 params) for efficiency                         │
│                          │ - Add alternating two-qubit interactions with different parameter layers to increase      │
│                          │ expressiveness                                                                            │
│                          │ - Introduce YY and ZZ gates alongside XX to create richer entanglement patterns           │
│                          │ - Implement a multi-layer structure with varied gate combinations to capture complex      │
│                          │ decision boundaries                                                                       │
│                          │ - Use separate rotation parameters for different stages to allow the optimizer            │
│                          │ flexibility for hard samples                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This balances:                                                                            │
│                          │ - Parameter economy (still 3-4 distinct params)                                           │
│                          │ - Expressiveness (varied gate types and patterns)                                         │
│                          │ - Generalization (simple shared structure)                                                │
│                          │ - Hard sample separation (layered interactions with multiple rotation angles)             │
