│ patch_name               │ diversified_ising_ansatz                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses excessive parameter sharing (3 distinct params) which severely    │
│                          │ limits model capacity. The second program achieved 0.58 score by using differentiated     │
│                          │ parameters (10 distinct params) with individualized XX/YY/ZZ gates, much better           │
│                          │ worst_group_margin (0.28 vs 0.00) and validation accuracy (0.97 vs 0.58).                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The strategy is to:                                                                       │
│                          │ 1. Keep RY gates but with better differentiation (alternating or qubit-specific)          │
│                          │ 2. Add back RZ pre gates (removed in current)                                             │
│                          │ 3. Use diverse Ising gate types (XX, YY, ZZ) on different qubit pairs with individual     │
│                          │ parameters to allow the model to learn specialized interactions                           │
│                          │ 4. Add post-layer RZ gates for phase adjustment                                           │
│                          │ 5. Keep total distinct params moderate (~8-10) for good generalization                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This balances expressiveness (needed to separate hardest samples) with parameter economy  │
│                          │ (essential for generalization from small training set).                                   │
