│                          │ (4) zz_param for all ZZ gates, and (5) rz_param for all Z-rotations. This maintains the   │
│                          │ proven architectural strength—alternating single-qubit gates, diverse Ising interactions, │
│                          │ and cross-qubit couplings—that achieved 96% test accuracy and 0.28 worst-group margin,    │
│                          │ while dramatically improving parameter efficiency. The parameter economy boost should     │
│                          │ outweigh any minor accuracy loss from sharing, since the scoring heavily penalizes        │
│                          │ distinct parameter count with no diminishing returns. The circuit retains sufficient      │
│                          │ expressivity through the two-pattern RY alternation and the diversity of Ising gate types │
│                          │ (XX, YY, ZZ) despite sharing within each type.                                            │
