│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the best aspects of the three prior programs:                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **From the best performer (score 0.58)**: Uses the parameter separation strategy with  │
│                          │ `rz_pre` and `rz_post` for RZ rotations, which achieved excellent validation accuracy     │
│                          │ (0.97) and worst_group_margin (0.28). This approach provides better expressiveness        │
│                          │ through separated pre- and post-processing RZ layers.                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **From the current program (score 0.44)**: Uses the alternating XX entanglement        │
│                          │ pattern with even/odd parameter sharing that provided good two-qubit gate connectivity.   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **From the seed program (score 0.46)**: Inspired by the use of diverse two-qubit gates │
│                          │ (XX, YY, ZZ) which provide richer expressiveness for capturing problem structure.         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Key improvements in this hybrid:**                                                      │
│                          │ - Reduces parameter count from 12 to 10 distinct parameters (better parameter efficiency) │
│                          │ - Maintains the proven `rz_pre`/`rz_post` separation that delivered the best validation   │
│                          │ accuracy                                                                                  │
│                          │ - Uses alternating XX gates with parameter sharing for structured entanglement            │
│                          │ - Simplifies single-qubit rotations to just 2 shared parameters (ry_even/ry_odd) to       │
│                          │ reduce overfitting                                                                        │
│                          │ - Removes the extra RZ layers that add depth without benefit                              │
│                          │ - Total gate count remains efficient at around 86 gates                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This design should generalize better while maintaining good separation on hard samples    │
│                          │ through the pre/post RZ strategy.                                                         │
