│ patch_name               │ deepened_ising_block_reuse                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Analysis of prior programs shows that the second program achieves the best combined score │
│                          │ (0.58) with strong validation accuracy (0.97), test accuracy (0.96), and good             │
│                          │ worst_group_margin (0.28). It uses 10 distinct parameters with a structured approach:     │
│                          │ alternating ry_0/ry_1 pattern, shared rz_pre, and a balanced mix of XX/YY/ZZ gates with   │
│                          │ strategic parameter reuse.                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current program (score 0.43) struggles with poor validation margin (0.09) and         │
│                          │ worst_group_margin (0.05), indicating it fails on hard samples. The issue is likely       │
│                          │ insufficient entanglement depth and poor parameter organization for robust separation.    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Following the recommendation to deepen entanglement through Ising block duplication with  │
│                          │ parameter reuse, I will:                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Start with the proven structure from program 2 (ry_0/ry_1 alternation, rz_pre on all   │
│                          │ qubits)                                                                                   │
│                          │ 2. Apply the first Ising layer: XX([0,1]), YY([2,3]), ZZ([4,5]), XX([6,7]), YY([1,4]),    │
│                          │ ZZ([3,6])                                                                                 │
│                          │ 3. Duplicate this exact layer with parameter reuse to intensify correlation capture       │
│                          │ 4. Add rz_post on all qubits for final rotation                                           │
│                          │ 5. Keep n_distinct_params at 10 to satisfy parameter economy requirement                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This maintains depth in the 15-18 sweet spot while achieving deeper entanglement patterns │
│                          │ that should capture hard examples better and improve worst_group_margin.                  │
