│ patch_name               │ dual_ising_reuse                                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ This approach implements two sequential layers of Ising two-qubit gates with strategic    │
│                          │ parameter reuse. The first layer applies XX, YY, and ZZ gates on adjacent qubit pairs,    │
│                          │ establishing local entanglement. The second layer reuses the same parameters on different │
│                          │ qubit pairs, creating long-range interactions and deeper entanglement. This dual-layer    │
│                          │ structure with parameter sharing balances three critical objectives: (1) sufficient       │
│                          │ expressiveness to separate hard samples (worst_group_margin), (2) parameter economy       │
│                          │ (fewer distinct params), and (3) generalization from small training sets. Unlike the      │
│                          │ current underfitted approach that over-shares parameters, this design provides rich       │
│                          │ two-qubit interactions while keeping the distinct parameter count at ~10, matching the    │
│                          │ highest-scoring prior program's efficiency.                                               │
