│ patch_name               │ mid_circuit_alternating_ry                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Insert a mid-circuit alternating RY layer before the final rz_post gates. This adds       │
│                          │ rotation gates on qubits [0,2,4,6] with parameter ry_even and on qubits [1,3,5,7] with    │
│                          │ parameter ry_odd, reusing the same parameters from the initial layer.                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This improves expressivity by:                                                            │
│                          │ 1. Providing additional rotation diversity in a different circuit phase                   │
│                          │ 2. Allowing the quantum circuit to learn more complex decision boundaries for hard        │
│                          │ samples                                                                                   │
│                          │ 3. Improving worst_group_margin (currently the critical bottleneck at 0.24)               │
│                          │ 4. NOT increasing distinct parameter count, only gate count                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The pattern matches the prior high-performing program which used distinct parameters for  │
│                          │ different pairs, and the recommendation specifically targets the robustness to hard       │
│                          │ samples through increased mid-circuit heterogeneity.                                      │
