│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ alternating_ry_mid_circuit                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves good parameter efficiency (5 distinct parameters) but        │
│                          │ suffers from poor generalization (gap of 0.21) and weak worst-group margin (0.25). The    │
│                          │ prior high-performing program (score 0.58) used 10 distinct parameters with an            │
│                          │ alternating RY pattern (ry_0 on even qubits, ry_1 on odd qubits) and achieved much better │
│                          │ validation margin (0.57) and worst-group margin (0.28).                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The structural redesign:                                                                  │
│                          │ 1. Returns to the proven alternating RY layer strategy (ry_0 and ry_1 parameters) applied │
│                          │ on all qubits at the start                                                                │
│                          │ 2. Adds a mid-circuit alternating RY layer before the final rotations to inject           │
│                          │ additional learnable heterogeneity at a critical point, following the recommendation      │
│                          │ 3. Introduces a pre-entanglement RZ layer to set phases before two-qubit interactions     │
│                          │ 4. Uses a diverse two-qubit entanglement pattern with XX, YY, and ZZ gates to create      │
│                          │ richer correlations                                                                       │
│                          │ 5. Concludes with a final alternating RY layer and post-RZ layer for readout preparation  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This structure:                                                                           │
│                          │ - Maintains the same input/output interface                                               │
│                          │ - Increases parameter diversity from 5 to 7 distinct parameters (ry_0, ry_1, rz_pre, xx,  │
│                          │ yy, zz, rz_post)                                                                          │
│                          │ - Creates three distinct "blocks" of alternating RY applications (initial, mid-circuit,   │
│                          │ final) to improve expressivity for difficult samples                                      │
│                          │ - Balances parameter economy with robust feature learning                                 │
│                          │ - Should improve worst-group margin by providing better discrimination capacity for hard  │
│                          │ samples                                                                                   │
