│ patch_description        │ This edit combines two improvements:                                                      │
│                          │ 1. Revert to the parameter-efficient RY sharing (ry_0/ry_1 alternating) that was proven   │
│                          │ effective in the best program (score 0.58)                                                │
│                          │ 2. Consolidate RZ rotations to use fewer distinct parameters                              │
│                          │ 3. Add long-range CRZ entanglers on diagonal qubit pairs [0,5], [1,6], [2,7], [3,4] using │
│                          │ a single shared parameter                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Rationale: The current program has poor worst_group_margin (0.18 vs best's 0.28).         │
│                          │ Long-range diagonal entanglers create global correlations that help separate hard         │
│                          │ examples. By adding these with parameter sharing and reverting to proven RY/RZ patterns,  │
│                          │ we gain:                                                                                  │
│                          │ - Better handling of difficult samples (worst-group margin improvement)                   │
│                          │ - Maintained parameter efficiency (only +1 distinct param)                                │
│                          │ - Symmetry across the 8-qubit system                                                      │
│                          │ - Global phase coherence through maximal qubit distances                                  │
