│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ hybrid_even_odd_ising_gates                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Analysis of the three candidates reveals clear performance patterns:                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Current program (score 0.44):** Poorest performer with 12 distinct parameters, low      │
│                          │ worst_group_margin (0.18), and poor validation_margin (0.44). The use of purely XX gates  │
│                          │ with no parameter diversity and individual RY gates for each qubit limits expressiveness. │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Prior program 2 (score 0.58):** Best performer using even/odd parameter sharing on RY   │
│                          │ gates (ry_0, ry_1) with diverse two-qubit gates (XX, YY, ZZ) on different qubit pairs.    │
│                          │ Achieves 10 distinct parameters and excellent worst_group_margin (0.35).                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Crossover inspiration (score 0.58):** Also achieves 0.58 with 8 distinct parameters     │
│                          │ (best parameter efficiency) through careful even/odd sharing (ry_even, ry_odd) and mixed  │
│                          │ gate types (XX, YY, ZZ), but has two RY blocks suggesting some redundancy.                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The crossover strategy combines:                                                          │
│                          │ 1. **Even/odd RY parameter sharing** from both top performers (ry_even for qubits 0,2,4,6 │
│                          │ and ry_odd for qubits 1,3,5,7) - proven superior to individual parameters                 │
│                          │ 2. **Mixed two-qubit gates** (XX on [0,1],[6,7]; YY on [2,3],[1,4]; ZZ on [4,5],[3,6])    │
│                          │ from the inspiration - this diversity outperforms uniform XX gates                        │
│                          │ 3. **Single RY block** (not repeated) - keeping the structure simpler than inspiration to │
│                          │ reduce depth while maintaining gate diversity                                             │
│                          │ 4. **Shared pre/post RZ parameters** (rz_pre, rz_post) from top performers                │
│                          │ 5. **Minimal gate count** while maintaining diversity and separation capability           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This yields 8 distinct parameters (best parameter efficiency score of 0.09 matches the    │
│                          │ best prior), reduced depth, and preserves the robust worst_group_margin performance.      │
