│                          │ 1. The current program over-aggregates parameters (only 6 distinct params), leading to    │
│                          │ severe underfitting: validation accuracy drops to 0.79, test to 0.77, with                │
│                          │ worst_group_margin at only 0.21.                                                          │
│                          │ 2. Prior Program 1 achieves 0.58 score with 8 distinct params, separating RZ pre/post     │
│                          │ phases and maintaining parameter economy while achieving 0.93 validation accuracy and     │
│                          │ 0.35 worst_group_margin.                                                                  │
│                          │ 3. Prior Program 2 achieves 0.58 score with 10 distinct params, using fully independent   │
│                          │ RY parameters and independent Ising gate parameters - better generalization (0.04 gap)    │
│                          │ and higher test accuracy (0.96).                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The crossover strategy:                                                                   │
│                          │ - Adopt the RY parameter differentiation from Prior Program 2 (ry_0, ry_1) instead of     │
│                          │ (ry_even, ry_odd) naming - this improves clarity and matches the better-performing        │
│                          │ architecture                                                                              │
│                          │ - Keep the critical RZ pre/post separation from Prior Program 1 (rz_pre vs rz_post) which │
│                          │ prevents parameter over-aggregation and enables the model to learn distinct               │
│                          │ transformations at different circuit stages                                               │
│                          │ - Use independent Ising gate parameters (xx_01, yy_23, zz_45, xx_67, yy_14, zz_36) from   │
│                          │ Prior Program 2 instead of shared parameters - this provides sufficient expressivity for  │
│                          │ robust separation                                                                         │
│                          │ - This yields 10 distinct parameters, matching Prior Program 2's parameter efficiency     │
│                          │ while maintaining the proven structure that achieves 0.58 score                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This balances expressivity (avoiding the current program's severe underfitting) with      │
│                          │ parameter economy (matching the best prior performance).                                  │
