│ patch_name               │ split_rz_pre_by_parity                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Split the pre-entanglement RZ layer into two parameters based on qubit parity, mirroring  │
│                          │ the successful alternating RY pattern. This restores heterogeneity in the initial phase   │
│                          │ preparation, which is critical for robust separation of hard samples                      │
│                          │ (worst_group_margin). The current monolithic rz_pre lacks expressiveness to capture       │
│                          │ qubit-specific rotation needs. By using rz_pre_even on qubits [0,2,4,6] and rz_pre_odd on │
│                          │ [1,3,5,7], we add only one new distinct parameter (7→8) while significantly improving the │
│                          │ model's ability to handle diverse sample difficulties, particularly the worst-case        │
│                          │ groups.                                                                                   │
