│ patch_description        │ The second program achieved superior performance (score 0.58 with test_accuracy 0.96,     │
│                          │ generalization_gap 0.04) using distinct parameters for each two-qubit gate                │
│                          │ (n_distinct_params=10). The current program reduced this to 8 by sharing xx_nn and        │
│                          │ yy_shared, but performance degraded (test_accuracy 0.89, generalization_gap 0.11).        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Empirical results demonstrate that parameter economy should not override generalization   │
│                          │ quality. The recommendation to further reduce parameters contradicts observed results. I  │
│                          │ propose restoring the distinct two-qubit parameters (xx_01, xx_67, yy_23, yy_14) to       │
│                          │ recover the superior generalization characteristics of the second program while keeping   │
│                          │ the current program's beneficial structure (extra RY layer and even/odd sharing in        │
│                          │ single-qubit gates).                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This balances parameter efficiency (still 10 distinct, not 12) with superior              │
│                          │ generalization and worst-group margin performance.                                        │
