                         Patch Metadata - Gen 31/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ restore_initial_ry_add_mid_rz                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The current program regressed by removing the initial RY parity layer that was present in │
│                          │ the first prior program (which scored 0.58). The initial parity-based RY layer with       │
│                          │ parameters alternating between ry_0 (even wires) and ry_1 (odd wires) is critical for     │
│                          │ robust separation of hard samples and better generalization.                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Additionally, insert a mid-circuit shared RZ layer (rz_mid applied to all 8 qubits) after │
│                          │ the two-qubit interaction block. This adds expressivity to the circuit's middle section   │
│                          │ without introducing new distinct parameters - the rz_mid parameter is reused across all   │
│                          │ qubits.                                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This restores the proven structure from the first prior program while adding one new      │
│                          │ distinct parameter (rz_mid), keeping us well within the n_distinct≤12 sweet spot.         │
│                          │ Expected improvements:                                                                    │
│                          │ - Worst_group_margin_mean: 0.27 → ~0.35+ (restore robustness)                             │
│                          │ - Validation_margin_mean: 0.50 → ~0.57-0.60 (restore separation)                          │
│                          │ - Generalization_gap_mean: 0.14 → ~0.04-0.11 (better held-out performance)                │
│                          │ - Combined score: 0.54 → ~0.58+                                                           │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
