│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ midcircuit_parity_swapped_ry_rz                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The current program added CRZ gates that increased n_distinct_params to 11 and degraded   │
│                          │ performance (score 0.50 vs prior 0.58). Instead of controlled gates, insert a mid-circuit │
│                          │ parity-swapped RY layer followed by a shared RZ gate, mirroring the proven                │
│                          │ parity-alternating structure from Prior Program 2 but with the parity roles reversed      │
│                          │ mid-circuit.                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach:                                                                            │
│                          │ 1. Adds only ONE new distinct parameter (rz_mid), keeping the parameter count lean        │
│                          │ 2. Provides mid-circuit expressivity and potential information mixing                     │
│                          │ 3. Uses the same proven parity pattern that worked well in Prior Program 2                │
│                          │ 4. Removes the problematic CRZ gates to restore generalization                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The insertion point is after the XX/YY/ZZ blocks and before the final rz_post gates,      │
│                          │ creating a natural "breathing" point in the circuit with symmetry.                        │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
