                         Patch Metadata - Gen 37/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_diagonal_crz_entangler                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Add a long-range shared-parameter CRZ entangler layer on diagonal qubit pairs immediately │
│                          │ before the final rz_post layer. This implements the recommendation to use diagonal CRZ    │
│                          │ gates [(0,5),(1,6),(2,7),(3,4)] with a single shared parameter.                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The rationale:                                                                            │
│                          │ - Diagonal pairs create long-range entanglement that complements existing                 │
│                          │ nearest-neighbor and mid-range interactions                                               │
│                          │ - Sharing one parameter keeps the trainable parameter count at 11 distinct params,        │
│                          │ improving parameter efficiency                                                            │
│                          │ - Long-range entanglers have shown empirically strong gains for separating difficult      │
│                          │ samples (worst_group_margin)                                                              │
│                          │ - Positioned before rz_post allows final RZ rotations to process the entangled state      │
│                          │ - Prior experiments showed these couplings improve test accuracy without overfitting      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected improvements:                                                                    │
│                          │ - Better worst_group_margin (currently 0.32, should approach 0.37+ from Program 1)        │
│                          │ - Maintained or improved generalization despite slightly increased expressivity           │
│                          │ - Lower convergence steps due to better circuit structure                                 │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0115                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5                                                     │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
│ diff_summary             │ added: 4; deleted: 0; modified: 0;                                                        │
