│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_diagonal_crz_entangler                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Add a long-range shared-parameter CRZ entangler layer immediately before the final RZ     │
│                          │ post-processing layer. The CRZ gates act on diagonal qubit pairs [(0,5), (1,6), (2,7),    │
│                          │ (3,4)] using a single shared parameter "crz_diag".                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This change is motivated by:                                                              │
│                          │ 1. The recommendation explicitly suggests this modification based on prior                │
│                          │ diversification of parametrized two-qubit couplings                                       │
│                          │ 2. Long-range entanglement provides stronger coupling for difficult-to-separate samples   │
│                          │ (worst group margin improvement)                                                          │
│                          │ 3. Single shared parameter adds minimal parameter overhead (10→11 distinct params, same   │
│                          │ as successful prior programs)                                                             │
│                          │ 4. Diagonal pairs provide complementary connectivity beyond nearest-neighbor and          │
│                          │ previously used pairs                                                                     │
│                          │ 5. CRZ parametrized gates showed strength in prior program 2 (score 0.59 vs current 0.56) │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected improvements:                                                                    │
│                          │ - Increased worst_group_margin_mean (critical for robust separation)                      │
│                          │ - Better generalization on held-out test samples                                          │
│                          │ - Faster convergence due to richer entanglement structure                                 │
