│ patch_name               │ add_diagonal_crz_entangler                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The best performing program (score 0.59) achieves strong validation and test accuracy but │
│                          │ has a relatively low worst_group_margin (0.31), indicating poor separation of the hardest │
│                          │ samples. The recommendation suggests adding diagonal CRZ entanglers with a shared         │
│                          │ parameter can improve worst-group margins without deepening the circuit unnecessarily.    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I will revert to the simpler, high-performing structure (program 2) and inject a diagonal │
│                          │ CRZ entangler layer immediately before the final rz_post layer. This uses four long-range │
│                          │ CRZ gates on diagonal pairs [(0,5), (1,6), (2,7), (3,4)] with a single shared parameter   │
│                          │ `crz_diag`, adding minimal complexity (4 gates, 1 parameter) while providing the          │
│                          │ long-range entanglement that appears to help separate difficult validation groups.        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach:                                                                            │
│                          │ 1. Keeps the simpler, proven structure that converges quickly and efficiently             │
│                          │ 2. Adds targeted long-range entanglement on diagonal pairs (less explored than            │
│                          │ nearest-neighbor)                                                                         │
│                          │ 3. Uses parameter sharing to maintain parameter efficiency (critical for scoring)         │
│                          │ 4. Should improve worst_group_margin while maintaining or improving overall score         │
