│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The second program (score 0.59) demonstrated better generalization with parametrized      │
│                          │ two-qubit gates (CRX, CRY) instead of Ising gates. This architecture had:                 │
│                          │ - Better accuracy on validation (0.97) and test (0.95)                                    │
│                          │ - Smaller generalization gap (0.05 vs 0.16)                                               │
│                          │ - Faster convergence (90 vs 510 steps)                                                    │
│                          │ - Fewer distinct parameters (10 vs 11)                                                    │
│                          │ - Comparable worst_group_margin (0.31)                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Strategy: Revert to the proven simpler architecture that uses CRX/CRY gates, which have   │
│                          │ shown better generalization and convergence properties. This removes the problematic      │
│                          │ diagonal CRZ layer and reduces model complexity to improve out-of-sample performance.     │
