│ patch_name               │ diagonal_crz_entangler                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ The current implementation achieves a score of 0.57 but suffers from a relatively large   │
│                          │ generalization gap (0.10) and modest worst-group margin (0.37). The recommendation        │
│                          │ suggests adding long-range CRZ entangling gates on diagonal pairs before the final        │
│                          │ post-rotation layer to improve worst-group separation without increasing parameters       │
│                          │ significantly.                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach recognizes that:                                                            │
│                          │ 1. The worst-group margin (0.37) is the bottleneck—the hardest samples need better        │
│                          │ separation                                                                                │
│                          │ 2. The generalization gap (0.10) indicates overfitting to training data rather than       │
│                          │ learning robust features                                                                  │
│                          │ 3. Long-range diagonal entanglers create non-local correlations that help distinguish     │
│                          │ difficult samples                                                                         │
│                          │ 4. Parameter sharing (single `crz_diag` parameter across four diagonal pairs) minimizes   │
│                          │ parameter count while maximizing expressiveness                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ By inserting CRZ gates on diagonal pairs [(0,5), (1,6), (2,7), (3,4)] with a shared       │
│                          │ parameter before the final RZ layer, we create a rich entanglement structure that bridges │
│                          │ the qubit space more effectively than the current nearest-neighbor interactions. This     │
│                          │ enables the circuit to form decision boundaries that robustly separate hard-to-classify   │
│                          │ samples without overfitting.                                                              │
