                         Patch Metadata - Gen 47/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ dual_ising_entangler_light                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The current program suffers from overfitting (16% generalization gap) and slow            │
│                          │ convergence (510 steps). Analysis of prior programs shows that:                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Gen 2 success**: Simpler architectures with 10 distinct params and depth 15 achieved │
│                          │ score 0.59 with better generalization (5% gap)                                            │
│                          │ 2. **Parameter sharing insight**: Reusing parameters reduces parameter count and improves │
│                          │ generalization without sacrificing expressivity                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Entangler diversity**: The prior successful program used 6 distinct two-qubit        │
│                          │ interactions (XX, YY, ZZ with different wirings)                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current program adds CRZ gates with full parameter sharing, which appears to increase │
│                          │ training difficulty without improving robustness to hard samples (worst_group_margin      │
│                          │ stuck at 0.30).                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Novel approach**: Return to the lean, high-performing structure from Gen 2 (6 Ising     │
│                          │ entanglers) but expand the entangler set by two additional distinct links as recommended: │
│                          │ ZZ on [0,3] and XX on [2,7]. This creates an 8-parameter two-qubit layer that:            │
│                          │ - Maintains lean parameter count (~11 distinct params)                                    │
│                          │ - Provides richer connectivity for worst-group separation                                 │
│                          │ - Keeps depth moderate (~17 steps)                                                        │
│                          │ - Removes the problematic CRZ diagonal layer that increased convergence time              │
│                          │ - Uses only proven Ising gates (XX, YY, ZZ) with independent parameters                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The structure interleaves single-qubit rotations (RY/RZ) with diverse two-qubit           │
│                          │ entanglers, allowing the circuit to learn both local and global correlations efficiently  │
│                          │ without overfitting.                                                                      │
