│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ expand_ising_entanglers_diag                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz has decent parameter efficiency (10 distinct params) but is showing a  │
│                          │ train-test gap (0.05→0.10 in generalization). The recommendation suggests expanding the   │
│                          │ Ising entangler set with two diagonal connections: ZZ[0,3] and XX[2,7]. This improves the │
│                          │ qubit coupling graph coverage from a bipartite-like structure to include longer-range     │
│                          │ interactions, which helps the classifier separate difficult samples better (improving     │
│                          │ worst_group_margin). Historical data shows this transition (6→8 unique two-qubit params   │
│                          │ at similar depths) tightens worst-group margins and lifts test accuracy. We add only 2    │
│                          │ new distinct parameters, so parameter efficiency remains competitive while robustness     │
│                          │ improves.                                                                                 │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0104                                                                                   │
