╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ dual_stage_shared_rz                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves 0.57 score with a 0.10 generalization gap and poor           │
│                          │ worst_group_margin (0.37). The prior best program (score 0.59) uses parametrized          │
│                          │ two-qubit gates (CRX, CRY) instead of pure Ising gates, suggesting that controlled gates  │
│                          │ provide better expressivity.                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key observations:                                                                         │
│                          │ 1. Best prior (0.59) uses CRX + CRY + mixed Ising, achieving better worst_group_margin    │
│                          │ (0.31) and lower generalization_gap (0.05)                                                │
│                          │ 2. Current program (0.57) has worse generalization_gap (0.10) and worst_group_margin      │
│                          │ (0.37), suggesting underfitting or poor robustness on hard samples                        │
│                          │ 3. The recommendation suggests stacking two shallow four-stage mini-blocks with SHARED    │
│                          │ phase parameters (rz_pre and rz_post)                                                     │
│                          │ 4. Parameter economy is critical: fewer distinct parameters ALWAYS scores higher          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Strategy:                                                                                 │
│                          │ - Create two identical shallow blocks, each with: RY → RZ_pre → [Ising + CR gates] →      │
│                          │ RZ_post                                                                                   │
│                          │ - Tie BOTH rz_pre and rz_post across both blocks to maintain ~12 distinct parameters      │
│                          │ total                                                                                     │
│                          │ - Use parametrized two-qubit gates (CRX, CRY, CRZ) mixed with Ising gates for better      │
│                          │ expressivity                                                                              │
│                          │ - Keep the efficient gate patterns from prior best program but structure as two repeated  │
│                          │ stages                                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This achieves:                                                                            │
│                          │ - Doubled effective circuit depth (two stages) to capture richer correlations             │
│                          │ - Parameter economy through cross-block parameter sharing                                 │
│                          │ - Better robustness on hard samples through increased expressivity                        │
│                          │ - Maintains ~12 parameters, ~0.08 efficiency                                              │
