│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ dual_block_mixed_gates_shared_phase                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ This edit implements a two-block structure inspired by the recommendation. The key        │
│                          │ insight from prior experiments is that Program 2 (score 0.59) achieved the best           │
│                          │ performance by:                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Mixing Ising gates (XX, YY, ZZ) with parametrized CR gates (CRX, CRY)                  │
│                          │ 2. Using moderate parameter sharing (10 distinct params)                                  │
│                          │ 3. Maintaining shallow depth with high expressiveness                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current program (score 0.47) suffers from over-regularization with only 5 distinct    │
│                          │ params, leading to poor generalization and low worst_group_margin (0.25 vs 0.31).         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit proposes doubling the circuit depth by stacking two identical block sequences,  │
│                          │ with:                                                                                     │
│                          │ - Each block: RY → RZ_pre →  → RZ_post                                                    │
│                          │ - SHARED rz_pre and rz_post across both blocks (keeping param count bounded)              │
│                          │ - Distinct Ising/CR parameters per block                                                  │
│                          │ - Total distinct params ≈ 12, efficiency ≈ 0.08, matching the high-performing program     │
│                          │ structure                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should capture richer correlations while preserving the generalization properties    │
│                          │ that made Program 2 successful.                                                           │
