│ patch_description        │ Add two new Ising entangler gates to expand qubit connectivity and improve worst-group    │
│                          │ margin separation:                                                                        │
│                          │ - ZZ gate on qubits [0,3] with param "zz_03"                                              │
│                          │ - XX gate on qubits [2,7] with param "xx_27"                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ These additions increase from 6 to 8 unique two-qubit gates, targeting previously         │
│                          │ unconnected qubit pairs (0-3 and 2-7). Historical data shows this expansion from Gen      │
│                          │ 31→36 tightened worst-group margins. The new gates are inserted in the entangler block    │
│                          │ after existing gates, maintaining the circuit structure while improving expressivity for  │
│                          │ hard-to-separate samples. Total distinct params increases from 11 to 13, but parameter    │
│                          │ efficiency gain from improved worst-group margin should outweigh the small overhead.      │
