│ patch_name               │ add_mid_circuit_parity_ry_rz                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Insert a mid-circuit parity-swapped RY + global RZ regularization block after the         │
│                          │ six-gate entangler and before the final rz_post stage. This adds three new parameters     │
│                          │ (ry_mid_0, ry_mid_1, rz_mid) with minimal overhead while leveraging the proven            │
│                          │ parity-alternating structure. The odd qubits (1,3,5,7) and even qubits (0,2,4,6) get      │
│                          │ different RY parameters, mirroring the front-end parity motif, followed by a broadcast RZ │
│                          │ on all qubits. This should improve worst_group_margin and robustness to hard samples      │
│                          │ without pushing total parameter count beyond the sweet spot.                              │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
