│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_long_range_crz_diagonal                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Analysis of the current program reveals:                                                  │
│                          │ 1. **Current score (0.56)** is lower than prior best (0.59), indicating recent changes    │
│                          │ hurt performance                                                                          │
│                          │ 2. **Worst-group margin (0.32)** is the critical bottleneck—this drives the combined      │
│                          │ score via robust separation                                                               │
│                          │ 3. **High convergence_step_mean (630)** vs prior (90) suggests the circuit struggles to   │
│                          │ optimize efficiently                                                                      │
│                          │ 4. **Generalization gap increased** from 0.05 to 0.10, indicating overfitting on training │
│                          │ set                                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight from the recommendation and prior work: adding long-range entanglement    │
│                          │ with a single shared parameter can improve worst-group margin without sacrificing         │
│                          │ parameter efficiency.                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Current circuit has local nearest-neighbor interactions (0-1, 2-3, 4-5, 6-7) but lacks    │
│                          │ diagonal long-range coupling. The proposal adds CRZ gates on diagonal pairs [(0,5),       │
│                          │ (1,6), (2,7), (3,4)], all sharing a single parameter `crz_diag`. This:                    │
│                          │ - Creates long-range connectivity that helps the circuit distinguish hard samples         │
│                          │ - Uses only ONE additional distinct parameter (maintaining efficiency)                    │
│                          │ - Improves worst-group margin by providing complementary entanglement structure           │
│                          │ - Should reduce convergence time by enabling richer feature space with minimal parameter  │
│                          │ overhead                                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The CRZ gates are inserted after `rz_mid` (middle of circuit) to provide mid-depth        │
│                          │ entanglement that can improve separation without early-circuit interference.              │
