│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ parity_split_rz_post                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current program scores 0.57, while the previous best (program 2) scored 0.59. The key │
│                          │ difference is that program 2 had better worst_group_margin (0.31 vs 0.30) and parameter   │
│                          │ efficiency (0.08 vs 0.07).                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation suggests splitting the global `rz_post` phase into two separate        │
│                          │ parameters based on even/odd qubit parity. This aligns with the even/odd symmetry already │
│                          │ present in the RY layer structure (ry_0 on even qubits, ry_1 on odd qubits), which has    │
│                          │ proven effective.                                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The proposed change:                                                                      │
│                          │ - Replace the shared `rz_post` parameter (applied to all 8 qubits) with two parameters:   │
│                          │ `rz_post_even` (on qubits 0,2,4,6) and `rz_post_odd` (on qubits 1,3,5,7)                  │
│                          │ - This increases distinct parameters from 11 to 12, but only by 1                         │
│                          │ - The refined phase control respects the underlying even/odd symmetry, improving          │
│                          │ robustness on hard samples (worst_group_margin)                                           │
│                          │ - This should reduce the generalization gap and improve separation on the hardest         │
│                          │ validation groups                                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This change maintains the circuit structure while adding targeted flexibility that        │
│                          │ leverages the demonstrated architectural bias toward even/odd separation.                 │
