                         Patch Metadata - Gen 55/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_diagonal_crz_entangler                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The current program has collapsed into over-simplified parameter sharing that severely    │
│                          │ hurts performance. The worst_group_margin dropped from 0.30-0.31 to 0.21, indicating the  │
│                          │ circuit cannot separate hard samples.                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The prior better-performing programs had:                                                 │
│                          │ 1. Separate RZ parameters for pre, mid, and post layers (not all shared)                  │
│                          │ 2. More diverse two-qubit gate types                                                      │
│                          │ 3. Better structure for expressivity                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation proposes adding long-range diagonal CRZ entanglers before the final    │
│                          │ rz_post layer. This adds only 1 parameter but creates non-local entanglement patterns     │
│                          │ that help with worst-group margin without increasing parameter count significantly.       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The fix:                                                                                  │
│                          │ 1. Restore the three-stage RZ structure (rz_pre, rz_mid, rz_post) instead of collapsing   │
│                          │ to one shared parameter                                                                   │
│                          │ 2. Add a CRZ entangler layer on diagonal qubit pairs [(0,5), (1,6), (2,7), (3,4)] with a  │
│                          │ single shared parameter before rz_post                                                    │
│                          │ 3. Keep the middle RY and two-qubit interaction structure similar to prior programs       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
