│ patch_description        │ The current program has 16 distinct parameters and a combined score of 0.57, while a      │
│                          │ prior simpler program achieved 0.59 with only 10 distinct parameters. The recommendation  │
│                          │ to add an initial global RZ layer aligns with improving phase flexibility without         │
│                          │ parameter explosion.                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key improvements:                                                                         │
│                          │ 1. Prepend 8 RZ gates with a shared parameter "rz_init" on all qubits - this provides     │
│                          │ global phase control at the start with only 1 new distinct parameter                      │
│                          │ 2. Consolidate to a single, well-tuned entangling block instead of two similar blocks -   │
│                          │ reduces depth and parameters while maintaining expressivity                               │
│                          │ 3. Use aggressive parameter sharing: keep ry_0 and ry_1 alternating pattern, and reuse    │
│                          │ the same entangling parameter names across structured positions                           │
│                          │ 4. This follows the successful structure from prior program 2 but enhances it with        │
│                          │ initial phase flexibility                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The initial RZ layer gives the optimizer extra degrees of freedom to tune global phases   │
│                          │ at low cost, improving convergence and robustness on hard samples (worst_group_margin).   │
│                          │ Fewer distinct parameters directly improves the score through parameter_efficiency        │
