│ patch_description        │ Return to program 2's efficient single-block structure (which scored 0.59) but enhance it │
│                          │ with parity-split RZ rotations on pre and post phases. This applies the recommendation by │
│                          │ splitting rz_pre into rz_pre_even and rz_pre_odd, and rz_post into rz_post_even and       │
│                          │ rz_post_odd. This adds only 2 parameters (10 to 12) while preserving the shallow depth    │
│                          │ (15) and maintaining the even/odd symmetry already present in the RY layer pattern. The   │
│                          │ controlled gate pattern (CRX, CRY, CRZ) from program 2 proved effective. This should:     │
│                          │ - Tighten the generalization gap through finer phase control                              │
│                          │ - Maintain parameter economy with only 12 distinct parameters                             │
│                          │ - Keep the fast convergence (90 steps)                                                    │
│                          │ - Improve robustness on hard samples by respecting the underlying even/odd symmetry       │
