│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ restore_expressivity_parity_midblock                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current program over-simplified by sharing too many parameters (only 6 distinct),     │
│                          │ leading to poor worst_group_margin (0.21) and validation accuracy (0.79). Prior program 2 │
│                          │ achieved 0.59 score with 10 distinct parameters and better worst_group_margin (0.31).     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key improvements:                                                                     │
│                          │ 1. Differentiate RZ gates using parity (rz_even/rz_odd) to match the RY parity encoding   │
│                          │ structure                                                                                 │
│                          │ 2. Split the two-qubit interaction parameters by gate type (xx_param, yy_param, zz_param  │
│                          │ separate) rather than sharing across different gate types                                 │
│                          │ 3. Insert a lightweight parity-based mid-circuit RY layer before final RZ to boost        │
│                          │ expressivity while keeping parameter count modest                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This restores expressivity for better robust separation on hard samples without excess    │
│                          │ parameter bloat, targeting ~9-10 distinct parameters and score ~0.58-0.60.                │
