│ patch_name               │ replace_crz_with_ising_simplify                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The current program introduces a CRZ diagonal entangler layer that performs poorly        │
│                          │ (convergence at 2160 steps vs 90 in prior program 2). CRZ gates with full parameter       │
│                          │ sharing appear to be a training bottleneck and cause worse worst_group_margin (0.28 vs    │
│                          │ 0.31).                                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Prior program 2 achieved better performance (0.59 score) using only Ising gates           │
│                          │ (XX/YY/ZZ) for two-qubit interactions, with 6 distinct 2-qubit couplings and no CRZ       │
│                          │ layer.                                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The fix:                                                                                  │
│                          │ 1. Replace the 4 CRZ diagonal gates with 4 Ising gates (ZZ) with unique parameters        │
│                          │ 2. Remove the redundant mid-circuit RZ layer (which appears to be less effective than the │
│                          │ pre/post RZ layers)                                                                       │
│                          │ 3. This reduces depth, improves convergence speed, and aligns with the proven prior       │
│                          │ architecture                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This maintains parameter efficiency while using gates that empirically train faster and   │
│                          │ achieve better margins on hard samples.                                                   │
