│                          │ gates, 1 parameter) on diagonal qubit pairs, which causes severe convergence issues (2160 │
│                          │ steps vs 90 in Program 2). The worst_group_margin also degraded significantly (0.28 vs    │
│                          │ 0.31).                                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Program 2 achieved the best score (0.59) with a cleaner structure using distinct Ising    │
│                          │ gate parameters (XX, YY, ZZ) on specific qubit pairs, avoiding the convergence pitfalls   │
│                          │ of the current design.                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit removes the problematic CRZ diagonal layer and restores the proven Ising        │
│                          │ interaction pattern from Program 2, which:                                                │
│                          │ - Eliminates the extreme parameter sharing that blocks gradient flow                      │
│                          │ - Uses targeted two-qubit couplings (0-1, 2-3, 4-5, 6-7, 1-4, 3-6) that have proven       │
│                          │ effective                                                                                 │
│                          │ - Simplifies the structure (fewer gates, better trainability)                             │
│                          │ - Restores the final RZ post-processing layer which contributes to margin quality         │
│                          │ - Expected to recover convergence speed and worst-group margin performance                │
