│                          │ Algorithmic approach:                                                                     │
│                          │ - Return to a simpler, proven architecture with minimal depth                             │
│                          │ - Use only 2 distinct RY parameters (parity-based alternation) for robustness             │
│                          │ - Single shared RZ pre-layer for computational universality                               │
│                          │ - Minimal two-qubit entanglement using mixed Ising gates (XX, YY, ZZ) on strategic pairs  │
│                          │ - Single post-layer RZ for final rotation                                                 │
│                          │ - Eliminate unnecessary CRX/CRY/CRZ layers that seem to add overfitting risk without      │
│                          │ proportional benefit                                                                      │
│                          │ - Target convergence in <150 steps, generalization gap <0.05, and worst_group_margin      │
│                          │ >0.32                                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This stripped-down design maximizes parameter efficiency (7-8 distinct params) while      │
│                          │ maintaining the proven expressivity needed for robust separation on hard samples.         │
