│ patch_name               │ add_longrange_ising_links                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Following the expert recommendation, add two long-range Ising coupling gates to improve   │
│                          │ connectivity diversity and robustness on harder samples (worst group margin). The current │
│                          │ circuit uses only nearest-neighbor and some mid-range entanglement. Adding explicit ZZ    │
│                          │ coupling between qubits 0-3 (widely separated) and XX coupling between qubits 2-7         │
│                          │ enriches the entangling structure without dramatically increasing depth or parameter      │
│                          │ count. This should improve worst_group_margin (currently 0.37, target >0.40) and reduce   │
│                          │ the generalization gap by enabling better feature extraction for difficult samples. The   │
│                          │ gates are added after the main entangler block but before the final post-rotations,       │
│                          │ maintaining a clean layer structure.                                                      │
