╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ pure_ising_return                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The current program suffers from shared CRZ parameters that degrade worst-group margin    │
│                          │ (0.30) and validation accuracy (0.88). The recommendation and prior results show that     │
│                          │ pure Ising gates (XX, YY, ZZ) with unique per-link parameters achieve better worst-group  │
│                          │ margin (0.34 in Seed 1).                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key parameter changes:                                                                    │
│                          │ - Remove CRZ diagonal gates (the shared "crz_diag" parameter is causing overfitting and   │
│                          │ poor generalization)                                                                      │
│                          │ - Use all 6 unique Ising parameters: xx_01, xx_67, yy_23, yy_14, zz_45, zz_36 (no sharing │
│                          │ on two-qubit gates)                                                                       │
│                          │ - Simplify single-qubit rotations: use just 2 distinct RY params and 2 distinct RZ params │
│                          │ - Keep the core architecture: RY layer → RZ layer → 6 Ising gates → RZ readout            │
│                          │ - Reduces distinct parameter count to 10 while maintaining the effective Ising structure  │
│                          │ proven to work                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should:                                                                              │
│                          │ 1. Restore worst-group margin by using unique parameters for each entangling link         │
│                          │ 2. Improve generalization by removing problematic shared CRZ gates                        │
│                          │ 3. Speed convergence by removing unnecessary diagonal gates                               │
│                          │ 4. Maintain parameter efficiency                                                          │
