│                          │ worst-group margin (0.31).                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Adding a 7th Ising gate on an uncovered pair [0,7] (connecting opposite ends of the qubit │
│                          │ chain) will:                                                                              │
│                          │ 1. Improve the entanglement structure by bridging previously disconnected regions         │
│                          │ 2. Better separate hardest samples (worst_group_margin metric)                            │
│                          │ 3. Reduce convergence steps (Gen 54: 90 vs Current: 480)                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The added gate uses a new unique parameter "xx_07" following the Ising gate naming        │
│                          │ convention. This increases n_distinct_params from 11 to 12, but the improvement in        │
│                          │ worst_group_margin should outweigh the small parameter cost, as evidenced by Gen 0's      │
│                          │ superior robustness despite having 12 parameters.                                         │
