│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ parity_split_rz_pre_post_with_mid                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Restore the proven four-stage block structure from prior program 1, which achieved score  │
│                          │ 0.58. The key improvements are:                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Split the global rz_pre into rz_pre_even (wires 0,2,4,6) and rz_pre_odd (wires         │
│                          │ 1,3,5,7) to mirror the ry_0/ry_1 alternation pattern                                      │
│                          │ 2. Reintroduce the rz_mid layer between the first and second RY stages, which provides    │
│                          │ better expressivity in the middle of the circuit                                          │
│                          │ 3. Split rz_post into rz_post_even and rz_post_odd (already present in prior program 1)   │
│                          │ 4. Alternate the RY parameters in the second RY stage (ry_1 on even wires, ry_0 on odd    │
│                          │ wires) to create symmetric expressivity                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This structure worked well in prior program 1 (score 0.58, convergence 120 steps,         │
│                          │ generalization_gap 0.05) and should improve upon the current program's poor convergence   │
│                          │ (180 steps) and large generalization gap (0.10).                                          │
