│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ shared_params_ising_hybrid                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the best characteristics from both high-performing programs:      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **From Current Program (0.59 score)**: The aggressive parameter sharing strategy       │
│                          │ (ry_0, ry_1 alternating pattern and shared rz_pre/rz_post) which achieves excellent       │
│                          │ parameter efficiency (10 distinct params) and faster convergence (90 steps). This         │
│                          │ demonstrates strong generalization with minimal overfitting.                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **From Second Prior Program (0.58 score)**: The structured two-qubit entanglement      │
│                          │ using diverse Ising gate types (XX, YY, ZZ) in specific qubit pairings, plus the          │
│                          │ alternating RY pattern after the first layer, which contributes to the high               │
│                          │ worst_group_margin (0.34).                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The hybrid approach:                                                                      │
│                          │ - Keeps the highly efficient 2-parameter RY sharing (ry_0, ry_1 alternating on all 8      │
│                          │ qubits)                                                                                   │
│                          │ - Uses single shared rz_pre for all qubits (parameter efficiency)                         │
│                          │ - Replaces mixed CRX/CRY gates with pure Ising gates (XX, YY, ZZ) in the same qubit pairs │
│                          │ - Adds a second RY layer with alternating pattern to increase expressivity without adding │
│                          │ parameters                                                                                │
│                          │ - Keeps shared rz_post for all qubits                                                     │
│                          │ - Removes unnecessary gates while maintaining the proven two-qubit entanglement structure │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should achieve:                                                                      │
│                          │ - Better worst_group_margin through diverse two-qubit interactions                        │
│                          │ - Maintained parameter efficiency (keeping ~10 distinct params)                           │
│                          │ - Improved robustness on difficult samples through structured entanglement                │
│                          │ - Faster convergence due to reduced parameter count                                       │
