                         Patch Metadata - Gen 75/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ enhanced_parity_with_dual_entangle                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves good parameter efficiency (8 distinct params) but shows      │
│                          │ degraded validation accuracy (0.91 vs 0.97 in prior programs) and increased               │
│                          │ generalization gap (0.11 vs 0.05). The key issue is that while parameter sharing reduces  │
│                          │ count, it may be over-constraining the model's expressiveness for the hardest samples.    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Analysis of prior programs:                                                               │
│                          │ 1. Seed 1 (0.58 score): 12 distinct params, complex mid-layer with RY swap and parity     │
│                          │ post-RZ                                                                                   │
│                          │ 2. Seed 2 (0.59 score, best): 10 distinct params, simpler architecture with CRX/CRY       │
│                          │ parametrized gates, faster convergence (90 steps)                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Current program (0.57 score): 8 params but worse validation accuracy and higher test      │
│                          │ loss.                                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key insight: Seed 2's use of parametrized two-qubit gates (CRX, CRY) instead of only      │
│                          │ Ising gates provides more flexible entanglement. The current program lacks this           │
│                          │ expressiveness.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ New approach:                                                                             │
│                          │ 1. Retain the proven parity-based RY layer (ry_even, ry_odd) for parameter economy        │
│                          │ 2. Replace some fixed Ising gates with parametrized CRZ gates to increase expressiveness  │
│                          │ without adding many params                                                                │
│                          │ 3. Add a second mid-layer entanglement block (similar to Seed 1's success with multiple   │
│                          │ entangling stages)                                                                        │
│                          │ 4. Use strategic parameter sharing: introduce 3 new CRZ params for flexible two-qubit     │
│                          │ control instead of 6 fixed Ising gates                                                    │
│                          │ 5. Keep the final RY parity + RZ post layers proven in current design                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This yields ~11-12 distinct params while recovering the validation accuracy through       │
│                          │ richer entanglement patterns.                                                             │
