│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ hybrid_entanglement_minimal                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the best-performing inspiration program (score 0.59) with         │
│                          │ selective improvements from the current program. The key insight is that the inspiration  │
│                          │ program achieves the highest score by:                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Using parametrized two-qubit gates (CRX, CRY) instead of pure Ising gates for specific │
│                          │ pairs, which provides better expressivity for difficult samples                           │
│                          │ 2. Maintaining minimal parameter count (10 distinct parameters) through aggressive        │
│                          │ parameter sharing                                                                         │
│                          │ 3. Using simpler single-parameter RZ post-layer instead of even/odd splitting             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current program uses even/odd parameter splitting for RY and RZ, which increases      │
│                          │ parameter count without improving performance. The inspiration program's approach of      │
│                          │ using only two base RY parameters (ry_0, ry_1) with alternating assignment and unified    │
│                          │ post-layer RZ is more parameter-efficient.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ However, I'll enhance this slightly by:                                                   │
│                          │ - Keeping the proven CRX/CRY structure from the best inspiration                          │
│                          │ - Testing if selective two-qubit entanglement coupling (XX on 0-1, ZZ on 4-5, etc.)       │
│                          │ combined with controlled parametrized gates works better                                  │
│                          │ - Maintaining the 10-distinct-parameter efficiency that drives the score                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The strategy: use the exact structure that achieved 0.59, as it dominates the current     │
│                          │ program (0.57) and should outperform it. This is a conservative but data-driven crossover │
│                          │ focused on the winning structure.                                                         │
