│                          │ with single shared `rz_post` (1 param), reducing distinct params from 12 to 11            │
│                          │ 2. Add long-range XX entangler between qubits 0 and 7 immediately after the main          │
│                          │ entangler block, which improves worst-group margins on hard samples as shown in prior     │
│                          │ generations                                                                               │
│                          │ 3. Remove the middle RZ layer (`rz_mid`) to further reduce parameter count to 10,         │
│                          │ matching the best prior version                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This aligns with the observation that parameter economy is critical: "fewer distinct      │
│                          │ trainable parameter names ALWAYS scores higher, with no point of diminishing returns."    │
│                          │ The worst_group_margin can be improved through better entanglement structure rather than  │
│                          │ adding layers.                                                                            │
