│ patch_description        │ Replace the ZZ gate at wires [4,5] with a CRZ gate to improve expressivity at this        │
│                          │ critical entangling link. The second prior program demonstrated that controlled           │
│                          │ parametrized gates (CRX, CRY) outperform simple Ising gates while maintaining parameter   │
│                          │ efficiency. This change applies the same principle to the [4,5] bottleneck which connects │
│                          │ the two halves of the circuit. CRZ provides controlled-phase rotation which should better │
│                          │ separate difficult samples (improving worst_group_margin from 0.27 to potentially 0.31+)  │
│                          │ without increasing parameter count.                                                       │
